After this PR, `recentSearchesMetadata` and `isRecentSearchesDataLoaded` in `SearchRouter` exist solely to compute the `isInitialDataLoading` prop for `SearchAutocompleteList`. The parent is acting as a data intermediary — subscribing to `ONYXKEYS.RECENT_SEARCHES` only to pass loading state to the child. `SearchAutocompleteList` already subscribes to the same Onyx key internally (line 177: `useOnyx(ONYXKEYS.RECENT_SEARCHES)`), so it can determine loading state itself.

Remove the `isInitialDataLoading` prop and let `SearchAutocompleteList` compute loading state internally:

```tsx
// Inside SearchAutocompleteList, replace the isInitialDataLoading prop with:
const [, recentSearchesMetadata] = useOnyx(ONYXKEYS.RECENT_SEARCHES, {canBeMissing: true});
const isRecentSearchesDataLoaded = \!isLoadingOnyxValue(recentSearchesMetadata);
const isLoading = \!isRecentSearchesDataLoaded || \!areOptionsInitialized;
```

This also allows removing `recentSearchesMetadata`, `isRecentSearchesDataLoaded`, and the `isLoadingOnyxValue` import from `SearchRouter`.

